{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1273739-looking-for-wod-players-to-do-live-play-in-greater-philadelphia-area","id":1273739,"title":"Looking for WoD players to do Live Play in Greater Philadelphia Area","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-10T09:34:14-08:00","id":1273739,"title":"Looking for WoD players to do Live Play in Greater Philadelphia Area","content":"Howdy! I'm one of the cohosts of Mage: The Podcast and we're looking to do something between a tutorial and a live play for Mage: The Ascension. The goal is to introduce people to WoD systems and less to provide a radioplay. While those are enjoyable, our goal is to really help people get up and running with a live example. I've always done chronicles face-to-face in meatspace and before I put out a call to use Roll20 or Discord I'm curious if there are enough players within the greater Philadelphia area that I could skip that.<br /> <br /> What I'm looking for:<br /> -Familiarity with at least one WoD system (the core stuff), if you're familiar with Mage, awesome.<br /> -Conversational English. You don't need to be a native speaker but should be able to discuss what's happening in the game in English.<br /> -Availability.<br /> -Plays well with others. I fully respect the player who picks an obtuse paradigm and is a loner, but this project wouldn't work for that person.<br /> -Proximity to Philadelphia. I'd be running this in meatspace preferably in Philly but if everyone is in NY or DC I can move but the NE corridor of the US is a must.<br /> <br /> If this completely fails, I'll be shifting to Discord or what have you but want to shoot for meatspace first.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","